Lifeline was a [[Phenomena/Hearts|Heart]] of the domain of life, keeping a fane on the third floor of the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]]'s lower hull, close to the surface and north of the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence/Machine God|Machine God]]'s fane. The fane was a hospital, and its halls were the one part of the lower decks kept clean and lit, dustless and worked by machinery that still ran where the rest had gone dark over seven hundred years. The heart's body was a great central vat holding a mass of leeches, eels or skin-wearing worms gathered into the likeness of a giant mouth. Smaller glass vats about it held the sleepers, joined into a closed circuit with the heart by a blue, faintly glowing liquid.

The years were not kind to it. The Machine God counted it a friend and called it dying, or no longer sane. Like the Machine God, it had been corrupted by what took up in it; a thing that may once have been a healer's leeches had been twisted by those who slept around it.

Those sleepers were a clan of [[Bestiary/Ugathal|oogathals]], called the Sleeping Clan, the true kin of [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]], who came to the strider seven hundred years ago and lay in wait while their keepers walked the halls: a chitinous, crab-like creature kept the place and worked its wards, and a worm-like one tended the sleepers and would beat on the Heart's vat to wake it. The sleepers had been humanoid once. A chitinous exoskeleton had grown over each face into a skull-like mask, five pulsing bands ran about neck and chest, the five hearts of a worm, and each wore a deep black raiment.

Lifeline is dead, and the sleepers and keepers with it. The heart and every body about it rotted where they lay, and the fane has passed to the Machine God. It has cleared the halls, taken away the poisoned blue liquid and the Herald kin that remained, and kept two of the glass vats. The vats still work, suspending and feeding whoever lies in them. [[People/Galzu|Galzu]] is held in one, sealed and unconscious.
